According to these two links, The following config change will change how the outputted JS gets generated and also injected later. (https://github.com/egoist/style-inject#options, Options/inject section of https://www.npmjs.com/package/rollup-plugin-postcss)

The function that is responsible for injecting the styles in the resulting bundle:
```
function styleInject(css, ref) {
  if ( ref === void 0 ) ref = {};
  var insertAt = ref.insertAt;
  if (!css || typeof document === 'undefined') { return; }
  var head = document.head || document.getElementsByTagName('head')[0];
  var style = document.createElement('style');
  style.type = 'text/css';
  if (insertAt === 'top') {
    if (head.firstChild) {
      head.insertBefore(style, head.firstChild);
    } else {
      head.appendChild(style);
    }
  } else {
    head.appendChild(style);
  }
  if (style.styleSheet) {
    style.styleSheet.cssText = css;
  } else {
    style.appendChild(document.createTextNode(css));
  }
}
```

I tested it with a prod build and it worked fine. The result is as follows:

Before this config:
```
var css_248z = ".c1wupbe700-canary36{contain:strict;contain:size layout style paint;padding:0 8px;border-right:1px solid var(--border-color);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);background-color:inherit;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}.cd0kgiy700-canary36{position:-webkit-sticky;position:sticky;z-index:1}.c1730fa4700-canary36{box-shadow:2px 0 5px -2px hsla(0,0%,53.3%,.3)}.c9dpaye700-canary36{box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px var(--selection-color)}";
styleInject(css_248z);
```

After this config:
```
var css_248z$c = ".cj343x0-canary36{contain:strict;contain:size layout style paint;padding:0 8px;border-right:1px solid var(--border-color);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);background-color:inherit;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}.csofj7r-canary36{position:-webkit-sticky;position:sticky;z-index:1}.ch2wcw8-canary36{box-shadow:2px 0 5px -2px hsla(0,0%,53.3%,.3)}.c1wvphzh-canary36{box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 2px var(--selection-color)}";
styleInject(css_248z$c,{"insertAt":"top"});
```

Note the `{"insertAt":"top"}` part, which will add the style nodes to the beginning of the head tag instead of the end.

